fix(phase5): relay-verbatim directive on guard-block responses

The M09192 question's first round of testing showed the LLM
paraphrasing the canned "no record" message into a generic
"no results, try again" reply. It lost the closest-matches hint
and made up a fake date range.

Fix: prepend a clear directive to the canned text that tells the
LLM to relay the message verbatim, in the user's language:

  [SZERVER-ŐRJELZÉS: A lenti szöveget SZÓ SZERINT idézd a
   felhasználónak, ne fogalmazd át. ...]
  [SERVER GUARD: Relay the text below VERBATIM to the user; do
   not paraphrase. ...]

Also stamp `_relay_verbatim: true` on the canned body so future
prompt-tuners can detect it programmatically.

Tests: 2 new cases in 20-result-guard.test.ts confirm the
directives are present in mcp-server.ts. Full suite: 326/326
(was 324), tsc clean.
